      <h2 class="section-title mb-8">Where we deliver</h2>
      <div class="prose-content max-w-4xl">
        <h3>United Arab Emirates</h3>
        <p>MEAICON's headquarters in Dubai anchors our regional operations. The UAE market combines mature telecom infrastructure, ambitious smart-city programmes, and stringent data residency requirements. We deliver enterprise connectivity, data centre builds, and 24/7 managed services across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, and the Northern Emirates — with local teams who understand federal procurement, free-zone regulations, and the operational expectations of government and financial-sector clients.</p>
        <h3>Saudi Arabia</h3>
        <p>Saudi Arabia is our fastest-growing market, driven by Vision 2030, giga-projects, and sovereign capability mandates. Our Riyadh and Jeddah teams deliver infrastructure for government entities, NEOM-tier developments, and the Kingdom's expanding financial sector. We understand local content requirements, Saudisation, and the compliance frameworks that govern public-sector technology procurement — and our designs account for the Kingdom's climate, scale, and sovereignty-first posture.</p>
        <h3>Qatar</h3>
        <p>Our Doha team serves government, banking, and energy-sector clients across Qatar. With a mature fibre infrastructure and a strong regulatory environment under ictQATAR, the market demands precision: zero-trust security architectures, Tier III/IV data centre standards, and operational rigour aligned to the 2022 FIFA World Cup legacy of mission-critical infrastructure. We deliver all three under one accountable model.</p>
        <h3>Oman</h3>
        <p>Oman's digital infrastructure is evolving rapidly, with Muscat as the hub and significant investment in smart-city and energy-sector connectivity. Our Muscat team delivers enterprise networks, security operations, and managed services for government and energy clients who operate in environments where fibre and satellite connectivity must coexist — and where OT/IT convergence for the energy sector is not optional.</p>
        <h3>Egypt</h3>
        <p>Cairo is our gateway to North African delivery. Egypt's large-scale telecom infrastructure, banking sector modernisation, and government digital transformation programmes require infrastructure that can scale from dense urban deployments to remote operational sites. Our Cairo team works with banks, telecom operators, and government agencies on network modernisation, security operations centres, and data centre consolidation.</p>
        <h3>Kenya</h3>
        <p>Nairobi is our East African hub — serving a market that leads the continent in mobile money, fintech, and cloud adoption. Our Kenyan team delivers connectivity for enterprise and financial-sector clients, security operations for banks and telecoms, and managed services that bridge the gap between urban fibre infrastructure and remote edge connectivity. Kenya's innovation ecosystem means we operate at the intersection of enterprise infrastructure and startup-grade agility.</p>
        <h3>Kuwait</h3>
        <p>Kuwait's push toward digital government and smart-city infrastructure creates demand for resilient connectivity and security operations. Our Kuwait City team delivers enterprise networks, cloud integration, and managed security services for government and financial-sector clients who require high availability and regulatory-grade compliance under Kuwait's e-government framework.</p>
        <h3>Bahrain</h3>
        <p>Bahrain's mature regulatory environment and fintech-first positioning make it a natural market for our security operations and data centre expertise. Our Manama team supports banks, insurance providers, and government entities with zero-trust architectures, compliance-driven monitoring, and infrastructure that meets the Central Bank of Bahrain's operational resilience standards.</p>
        <h3>India</h3>
        <p>Our India presence — across Mumbai, Bengaluru, and New Delhi — provides engineering depth, software development capability, and 24/7 operational support that backs our entire regional footprint. India is not a delivery back-office; it is an engineering centre where our network architects, security analysts, cloud engineers, and blockchain developers design, build, and operate infrastructure that runs across all eleven markets. The talent density and technical depth available in India directly enhance the quality of delivery in every market we serve.</p>
        <h3>Pakistan</h3>
        <p>Pakistan's rapidly digitising economy — with a booming fintech sector, expanding telecom infrastructure, and ambitious e-government initiatives — demands resilient connectivity and security operations. Our Islamabad and Karachi teams deliver enterprise networks, managed security services, and cloud integration for banks, telecom operators, and government agencies navigating the Digital Pakistan agenda. We understand the regulatory landscape under PTA and SBP, and we design infrastructure that performs reliably in markets where power resilience and fibre diversity are operational imperatives.</p>
        <h3>United States</h3>
        <p>Our US presence — across the Washington DC and New York metropolitan areas — anchors our North American operations and connects our regional delivery model to global technology vendors, cloud platforms, and capital markets. The US team provides vendor relationship management, procurement optimisation, and strategic account management for multinational clients whose infrastructure spans our our footprint and North America. This presence ensures that technology decisions made by global vendors — from cloud roadmaps to security platform features — are influenced by the operational realities of the markets we serve.</p>
